For each **Moira group** mailing list whose name **starts with “B”** (case-insensitive), compute the **distinct** number of members for each combination of: mailing list name, **owner**, **owner type**, and **member visibility** (treat member visibility as **“Public Members”** only when it is exactly public, and **“Hidden Members”** only when it is exactly not public; otherwise leave it **null/empty**).

Then, for each mailing list name, also include **rollup-style totals** that match a standard rollup on **(mailing list name, member visibility)**:
- include a **total row per visibility category** for that mailing list that **sums the per-owner distinct-member counts across all owners/owner types**; on these visibility-total rows, **leave owner and owner type null/empty**;
- **do not include a separate mailing-list grand-total row** that sums across all visibility categories (i.e., **no “all visibilities” total per mailing list**);
- **do not include any overall total across all mailing lists**.

**Exclude any rollup total rows whose summed member count is zero.** Order results by mailing list name, then by visibility.
